Why Is Demand Increasing
Defense Modernization: Naval forces are increasing AUV deployment for mine countermeasures, intelligence gathering, surveillance, and anti-submarine warfare.
Offshore Infrastructure: Oil and gas operators increasingly use AUVs for seabed mapping, pipeline inspection, and subsea infrastructure monitoring.
Technology Advancement: Better battery energy density, autonomous navigation, sensor integration, and AI-enabled decision-making are extending AUV mission capabilities.

Autonomous Underwater Vehicle Watch: AI-Enabled and Collaborative Operations
AUV development is moving toward longer endurance, greater autonomy, and collaborative operations. Advances in underwater acoustic networking, edge computing, navigation, and swarm coordination are enabling multiple vehicles to perform coordinated missions for defense, environmental monitoring, offshore inspection, and large-scale oceanographic surveys.

